{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/MigratingTo1.17","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to use the new "},{"code":"withSnapshotTesting","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" tool for customizing how snapshots are generated and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"diffs displayed."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/migratingto1.17"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This library is under constant development, and we are always looking for ways to simplify the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library, and make it more powerful. This version of the library has deprecated some APIs,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"introduced a new APIs, and includes beta support for Swift’s new native testing library.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Customizing snapshots","anchor":"Customizing-snapshots","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Currently there are two global variables in the library for customizing snapshot testing:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/isRecording"},{"text":" determines whether new snapshots are generated and saved to disk when the test","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"runs.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/diffTool"},{"text":" determines the command line tool that is used to inspect the diff of two files on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"disk.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"These customization options have a few downsides currently.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"First, because they are globals they can easily bleed over from test to test in unexpected ways.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"And further, Swift’s new testing library runs parallel tests in the same process, which is in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stark contrast to XCTest, which runs parallel tests in separate processes. This means there are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"even more chances for these globals to bleed from one test to another.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"And second, these options aren’t as granular as some of our users wanted. When ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/isRecording"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is true snapshots are generated and written to disk, and when it is false snapshots are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"generated, ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"unless","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" a file is not present on disk. The a snapshot ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"is","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" generated. Some of our","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"users wanted an option between these two extremes, where snapshots would not be generated if the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"file does not exist on disk.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"And the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/diffTool","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" variable allows one to specify a command line tool to use for visualizing","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"diffs of files, but only works when the command line tool accepts a very narrow set of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arguments,  _e.g.:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"sh","code":["ksdiff \/path\/to\/file1.png \/path\/to\/file2.png"]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Because of these reasons, the globals ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/isRecording","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/diffTool","type":"reference"},{"text":" are now deprecated, and we","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"have introduced a new tool that greatly improves upon all of these problems. There is now a function","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"called ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/withSnapshotTesting(record:diffTool:snapshotNaming:referenceStorage:locale:timeZone:calendar:operation:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for customizing snapshots. It","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"allows you to customize how the ","type":"text"},{"code":"assertSnapshot","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tool behaves for a well-defined scope.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Rather than overriding "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRecording"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"diffTool"},{"type":"text","text":" directly in your tests, you can wrap your test in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withSnapshotTesting"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"numberOfColumns":2,"columns":[{"content":[{"code":["\/\/ Before","","func testFeature() {","  isRecording = true ","  diffTool = \"ksdiff\"","  assertSnapshot(…)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}],"size":1},{"content":[{"code":["\/\/ After","","func testFeature() {","  withSnapshotTesting(record: .all, diffTool: .ksdiff) {","    assertSnapshot(…)","  }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}],"size":1}],"type":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you want to override the options for an entire test class, you can override the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"invokeTest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"method of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"XCTestCase"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"numberOfColumns":2,"columns":[{"content":[{"code":["\/\/ Before","","class FeatureTests: XCTestCase {","  override func invokeTest() {","    isRecording = true ","    diffTool = \"ksdiff\"","    defer { ","      isRecording = false","      diffTool = nil","    }","    super.invokeTest()","  }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}],"size":1},{"content":[{"code":["\/\/ After","","class FeatureTests: XCTestCase {","  override func invokeTest() {","    withSnapshotTesting(record: .all, diffTool: .ksdiff) {","      super.invokeTest()","    }","  }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}],"size":1}],"type":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"And if you want to override these settings for "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"all"}]},{"type":"text","text":" tests, then you can implement a base"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"XCTestCase"},{"type":"text","text":" subclass and have your tests inherit from it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Further, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"diffTool"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"record"},{"type":"text","text":" arguments have extra customization capabilities:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"diffTool"},{"text":" is now a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"function","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/DiffTool-swift.struct","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"function","type":"text"}]},{"text":"","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(String, String) -> String"},{"text":" that is handed the current snapshot file and the failed snapshot","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"file. It can return the command that one can run to display a diff. For example, to use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ImageMagick’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"compare"},{"text":" command and open the result in Preview.app:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["extension SnapshotTestingConfiguration.DiffTool {","  static let compare = Self { ","    \"compare \\\"\\($0)\\\" \\\"\\($1)\\\" png: | open -f -a Preview.app\" ","  }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"record"},{"text":" is now a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"type","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/Record-swift.struct","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"type","type":"text"}]},{"text":" with 4","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"choices: ","type":"text"},{"code":"all","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"missing","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"never","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"failed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"all"},{"type":"text","text":": All snapshots will be generated and saved to disk."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"missing"},{"text":": only the snapshots that are missing from the disk will be generated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and saved.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"never","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": No snapshots will be generated, even if they are missing. This option is appropriate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when running tests on CI so that re-tries of tests do not surprisingly pass after snapshots are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unexpectedly generated.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"failed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": Snapshots only for failing tests will be generated. This can be useful for tests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that use precision thresholds so that passing tests do not re-record snapshots that are","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"subtly different but still within the threshold.","type":"text"}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Beta support for Swift Testing","level":2,"anchor":"Beta-support-for-Swift-Testing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This release of the library provides beta support for Swift’s native Testing library. Prior to this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"release, using "},{"code":"assertSnapshot","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Test"},{"type":"text","text":" would result in a passing test no matter what. That is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"because under the hood "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assertSnapshot"},{"type":"text","text":" uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"XCTFail"},{"type":"text","text":" to trigger test failures, but that does not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cause test failures when using Swift Testing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In version 1.17 the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assertSnapshot"},{"type":"text","text":" helper will now intelligently figure out if tests are running"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"in an XCTest context or a Swift Testing context, and will determine if it should invoke ","type":"text"},{"code":"XCTFail","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Issue.record"},{"type":"text","text":" to trigger a test failure."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the most part you can write tests for Swift Testing exactly as you would for XCTest. However,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"there is one major difference. In order to override a snapshot’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration","type":"reference","isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"configuration","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"configuration","type":"text"}]},{"text":" for a particular test or an entire suite you","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"must use what are known as “test traits”:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import SnapshotTesting","","@Suite(.snapshots(record: .all, diffTool: .ksdiff))","struct FeatureTests {","  …","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"That will override the ","type":"text"},{"code":"diffTool","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"record","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" options for the entire ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureTests"},{"type":"text","text":" suite."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"These traits can also be used on individual "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Test"},{"type":"text","text":"s too."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SnapshotTesting"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Migrating to 1.17"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting"]]},"references":{"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/withSnapshotTesting(record:diffTool:snapshotNaming:referenceStorage:locale:timeZone:calendar:operation:)":{"title":"withSnapshotTesting(record:diffTool:snapshotNaming:referenceStorage:locale:timeZone:calendar:operation:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"withSnapshotTesting"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"R"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"record"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV6RecordV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Record"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"diffTool"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV8DiffToolV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DiffTool"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"snapshotNaming"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV0A6NamingO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SnapshotNaming"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"referenceStorage"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV16ReferenceStorageO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ReferenceStorage"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"locale"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation6LocaleV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Locale"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"timeZone"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation8TimeZoneV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TimeZone"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"calendar"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation8CalendarV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Calendar"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"operation"},{"kind":"text","text":": () "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"R"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"rethrows"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"R"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/withSnapshotTesting(record:diffTool:snapshotNaming:referenceStorage:locale:timeZone:calendar:operation:)","abstract":[{"text":"Customizes ","type":"text"},{"code":"assertSnapshot","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the duration of an operation.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/withsnapshottesting(record:difftool:snapshotnaming:referencestorage:locale:timezone:calendar:operation:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/SnapshotTestingConfiguration/Record-swift.struct":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/Record-swift.struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Record"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/snapshottestingconfiguration\/record-swift.struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Record"}],"title":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration.Record","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The record mode of the snapshot test."}]},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting":{"title":"SnapshotTesting","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting","abstract":[{"text":"Powerfully flexible snapshot testing.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting","type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/SnapshotTestingConfiguration":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration"}],"url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/snapshottestingconfiguration","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration","abstract":[{"text":"The configuration for a snapshot test.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration"},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/SnapshotTestingConfiguration/DiffTool-swift.struct":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DiffTool"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Describes the diff command used to diff two files on disk."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/DiffTool-swift.struct","title":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration.DiffTool","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"DiffTool","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/snapshottestingconfiguration\/difftool-swift.struct","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/diffTool":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/diffTool","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"diffTool","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"DiffTool","preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV8DiffToolV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Enhances failure messages with a command line diff tool expression that can be copied and pasted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"into a terminal."}],"url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/difftool","title":"diffTool","kind":"symbol","deprecated":true,"type":"topic"},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/isRecording":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether or not to record all new references."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/isRecording","url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/isrecording","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isRecording","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","deprecated":true,"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"isRecording"}}}